      {
        "id": 164128,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-03T12:21:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Kingofsouls\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/58f4c7/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Kingofsouls:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Tools return themselves to Fixers hand. So that's a no.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The rule book and video game implementation would disagree. &nbsp;Indestructible means the card can't leave play for any reason and that includes returning cards to your hand. &nbsp;You can test it yourself in the video game playing with Fixed Point from Time Catacylsm. &nbsp;Neither Fixer's tools or Omnitron-X's plating cards will return to your hand if you play another one while Fixed Point is out. &nbsp;</p>",
