      {
        "id": 164134,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-03T19:50:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>An interesting thing to note is that the first edition of Sentinels of the Multiverse did not have Into the Stratosphere ignore indestructible cards, in fact there are in indestructible cards in the base game. Spite gained the first Indestructible cards with his Drugs, which included the rule that they cannot be removed from paly by any means to esnure that Into the Stratosphere could not put them on top of the deck. After a little while though, people thought that they could use Into the Stratosphere to get rid of the drugs after Spite flipped. Since there are so many people who aren't aware that Indestructible includes removing cards from play by means other than destruction, Into the Stratosphere gained the \"non-indestructible\" requirement to help ensure people will not mis play Spite's Drugs or any other future Indestruble cards.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:45:17.281Z",
