      {
        "id": 164135,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-03T19:51:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don't think that it's counterintutive so much as just unintuitive. &nbsp;People look at \"indestructible\" and assume that it means \"cannot be destroyed\", and there's absolutely no reason to believe that it would do anything else unless you look it up in the rulebook, which most people won't do because there is already an obvious definition for the term, with no indication that further clarification would be necessary.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>What I would probably do would be to change \"Indestrutible\" to mean \"cannot be destroyed\" and errata Fixed Point to read \"All cards other than this card cannot leave play\" &nbsp;That preserves functionality while removing confusion.</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
