      {
        "id": 164140,
        "name": "Matchstickman",
        "username": "Matchstickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-04T10:38:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't think that it's counterintutive so much as just unintuitive. &nbsp;People look at \"indestructible\" and assume that it means \"cannot be destroyed\", and there's absolutely no reason to believe that it would do anything else unless you look it up in the rulebook,</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There are confusions with people asking if they can discard cards from play.</p>\n<p>Whatever the keyword used if you don't read the rules of a new game and apply logic from other games to it you are going to have problems.</p>",
        "post_number": 35,
        "post_type": 1,
